#!/usr/bin/env node
// The `nish` command, before `scripts/postinstall.mjs` has had a look at it.
//
// This file is deliberately tiny and deliberately not the whole story. On a
// machine that installed one of the prebuilt `@amritk/nish-<asset>` packages,
// postinstall replaces this file with a one-line `/bin/sh` exec of that
// package's native compiler, so nothing node-shaped is left in the path --
// measured at 3.2 ms against 94 ms for this shim, which is almost entirely
// node's own startup (docs/wp12-release.md, "What the launcher costs").
//
// It execs the binary in its own package rather than copying it here, because
// npm links the command through a symlink and the native compiler resolves
// `build.sh` and `runtime/` from argv[0] without following one. That section
// has the failure a copy produces.
//
// It has to keep working anyway, because the swap is a postinstall and
// `npm ci --ignore-scripts` is a normal thing for CI to do, as is a registry
// proxy or a sandbox that disables scripts outright. So this is the path that
// is always correct and sometimes slower, and the swap is the optimisation on
// top of it. Everything it delegates to is in `./launcher.js`, beside this
// file rather than in `dist/`: the command may not be a build artifact of the
// compiler it installs, and since 0.6.0 there is no `dist/` to build it into.
import "./launcher.js";
